1. [BLOCKER] src/formatter.rs:415 — bare `catch` with a body is silently dropped — `if let Some(var) = catch_var` is the only arm that writes `catch` and `format_block(catch_body)`; when `catch_var` is `None` but `catch_body` is non-empty the whole branch vanishes — `try/say 1/catch/say 2/end` formats to `try/say 1/end`, a semantic loss that breaks idempotence/losslessness — handle `None` by writing bare `catch` plus trailing comment plus `format_block(catch_body)`.
2. [MAJOR] src/formatter.rs:294 — empty `else` (`if !else_branch.is_empty()`) drops the `else` keyword, so `else // note` with an empty branch has nowhere to go and `write_keyword_line("end")` re-attaches it as `end // note` (same pattern at src/formatter.rs:430 for empty `finally`) — a trailing comment migrates off the line its author wrote it on with no test covering the empty-branch case — preserve the keyword when its line carries a comment, or claim the comment before dropping the keyword.
